iple phases and mechanisms, highlighting its complexity and the importance of understanding its implications for affected patients.\",31\r\n437,LOGOPEDA,\"A logopeda, also known as a logopedist or speech therapist, is a specialized professional dedicated to improving oral and swallowing functions in patients. They conduct various exercises and therapies aimed at enhancing speech and language abilities, as well as addressing swallowing disorders such as dysphagia. In particular, logopedas play a crucial role in the rehabilitation process for individuals experiencing swallowing difficulties. They also work with children to rehabilitate swallowing and feeding behaviors, helping to normalize oral stimulation. Overall, the logopeda's expertise encompasses a wide range of speech and language therapy, making them essential in the treatment and support of patients with communication and swallowing challenges.\",11\r\n440,FISIOLOGÍA,\"Fisiología refers to the study of bodily functions and processes, encompassing various aspects of human health and performance. It is particularly relevant in the context of nutrition and exercise performance, as it helps to understand how the body responds to different dietary and physical activities. Additionally, Fisiología includes the examination of specific functions such as swallowing and dysphagia, highlighting its importance in understanding both general bodily functions and specific health conditions.\",2\r\n61,BOLLO ALIMENTICIO,\"The \"\"BOLLO ALIMENTICIO\"\" refers to the mass of food that is formed in the mouth during the process of swallowing. This mass is created as food is chewed and mixed with saliva, and it is then transferred to the esophagus. The bolo alimenticio plays a crucial role in the digestive process, facilitating the movement of food from the mouth to the esophagus for further digestion.\",12\r\n456,VÍA AÉREA,\"VÍA AÉREA refers to the airway, which is the passage that connects the nose and mouth to the lungs. This structure is essential for proper respiratory function and plays a critical role in swallowing safety. Issues related to swallowing can significantly impact the airway, potentially leading to complications. Therefore, maintaining the integrity of the airway is vital for both breathing and safe swallowing.\",4\r\n997,EJERCICIOS DE POTENCIACIÓN DE LA LENGUA,\"\"\"EJERCICIOS DE POTENCIACIÓN DE LA LENGUA\"\" refers to a series of exercises specifically designed to improve the strength and mobility of the tongue. These exercises are essential for effective swallowing and overall oral function. One of the methods employed in these exercises involves the use of the Iowa Oral Performance Instrument (IOPI), a device that measures the pressure exerted by the tongue against the palate, thereby facilitating targeted training to enhance tongue strength.\",4\r\n457,BOL,\"BOL refers to the bolus, which is a mass of food or liquid formed in the mouth and subsequently swallowed. This process can be influenced by the viscosity of thickeners, which may alter the consistency of the bolus. The bolus plays a significant role in the study of swallowing mechanics, as it is the key element that is swallowed during the act of eating or drinking.\",3\r\n72,FARINGE,\"The entity \"\"FARINGE,\"\" also known as the pharynx, is a critical anatomical structure involved in the swallowing process. It is a muscular tube that connects the mouth and nasal passages to the esophagus, playing a vital role in the act of swallowing. The pharynx is assessed during procedures such as video fluoroscopy and VED (Videofluoroscopic Evaluation of Swallowing), highlighting its importance in evaluating swallowing function. Overall, the pharynx is an essential part of the throat that facilitates the transition of food and air, underscoring its significance in both respiratory and digestive systems.\",3\r\n326,PATIENCE,The patient is the individual undergoing assessment for swallowing capabilities and reactions to stimuli.,2\r\n465,ESFÍNTER ESOFÁGICO SUPERIOR,\"The \"\"ESFÍNTER ESOFÁGICO SUPERIOR\"\" is a muscle that plays a crucial role in controlling the entry of food into the esophagus. It is a functional unit involved in the process of swallowing, consisting of muscles that regulate the passage of food. This sphincter is particularly significant in the evaluation of oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects the ability to swallow.\",2\r\n467,RESIDUO,\"The term \"\"RESIDUO\"\" refers to the materials that remain in the body after the process of digestion, which can be significant in diagnostic studies of the digestive tract. Additionally, \"\"residue\"\" also pertains to the leftover food or liquid present in the pharynx following swallowing, which may indicate potential difficulties in swallowing. This dual definition highlights the importance of residue in both digestive health and the assessment of swallowing function.\",2\r\n439,ANATOMÍA,\"The study of the structure of the body, particularly relevant in understanding the swallowing process in patients with dysphagia.\",1\r\n770,CEREBRO HUMANO,El cerebro humano se activa por la percepción oral de la viscosidad y otras propiedades reológicas durante la deglución.,1\r\n89,NEUROANATOMÍA,,1\r\n441,TÉCNICAS DE MEJORA SENSORIAL,Techniques used to enhance sensory feedback during swallowing assessments and rehabilitation.,1\r\n442,MANIOBRAS DE DEGLUCIÓN,Specific maneuvers employed to improve swallowing safety and efficacy during assessments and treatments.,1\r\n464,OMNIPAQUE,\"Omnipaque is a non-ionic, monomeric, tri-iodinated, water-soluble radiological contrast medium used in diagnostic imaging.\",1\r\n469,ENFERMEDADES NEUROMUSCULARES,\"ENFERMEDADES NEUROMUSCULARES refers to a category of diseases that impact the muscles and their direct nervous control. These conditions may necessitate specialized nutritional approaches, particularly in pediatric care, to support the health and development of affected individuals.\",1\r\n466,PRUEBAS DIAGNÓSTICAS INSTRUMENTALES,Instrumental diagnostic tests are used to evaluate swallowing and identify any dysfunctions or abnormalities.,1\r\n468,FASES DE LA DEGLUCIÓN,\"The phases of swallowing include oral, pharyngeal, and esophageal phases, each critical for effective swallowing.\",1\r\n775,ELECTROENCEFALOGRAFÍA,,1\r\n772,IMÁGENES CEREBRALES,Los estudios funcionales cerebrales con imágenes indican que la sensación del gusto activa múltiples áreas cerebrales durante la deglución.,1\r\n774,MÉTODOS PSICOFÍSICOS,Los métodos psicofísicos son técnicas de evaluación que pueden ser utilizadas para estudiar la deglución y las propiedades sensoriales de los alimentos.,1\r\n68,LARINGE,\"La laringe es una parte fundamental del tracto respiratorio que desempeña un papel crucial durante la deglución, ya que se cierra para evitar que el bolo alimenticio ingrese a las vías respiratorias. Además, la laringe es una estructura anatómica que se evalúa durante la evaluación de la deglución (VED) debido a su importancia en este proceso. Su función en la deglución puede verse afectada por diversas condiciones que pueden llevar a la disfagia, un trastorno que dificulta la capacidad de tragar.\",2\r\n771,PROPIEDADES REOLÓGICAS,\"Las propiedades reológicas son características de los alimentos que afectan su textura y consistencia, influyendo en la percepción sensorial durante la deglución.\",2\r\n728,VISCOCIDAD,\"Viscosidad, or viscosity, is a rheological property that describes a fluid's resistance to flow. It plays a crucial role in the behavior of food boluses, influencing how they move and interact within the digestive system. Additionally, viscosity is a key factor in modifying the texture of liquids, particularly for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This modification is essential for ensuring that such patients can safely consume liquids without the risk of aspiration or choking.\",2\r\n773,ANÁLISIS DE PERFIL DE TEXTURA,El análisis de perfil