ining programs for patients.\",1\r\n459,ESFÍNTER ESOFÁGICO,\"The esophageal sphincter is a muscle that controls the passage of food from the esophagus into the stomach, important for swallowing safety.\",1\r\n458,VALLÉCULA,The vallecula is a space at the back of the throat that plays a role in swallowing and can be a site for food residue.,1\r\n67,ESÓFAGO,\"The esófago, or esophagus, is a muscular tube that plays a crucial role in the digestive system by transporting the bolus of food from the pharynx to the stomach during the process of swallowing. It is essential for the proper movement of food, and its function can be impacted by various swallowing disorders.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n1396,DEGLUCIÓN,PACIENTE,\"The entity \"\"DEGLUCIÓn\"\" refers to the act of swallowing, which is particularly relevant for \"\"PACIENTE\"\" (patients) experiencing dysphagia. Patients with dysphagia require assistance in performing the act of deglución through specific techniques designed to facilitate swallowing. As part of their treatment for oropharyngeal dysphagia, these patients must actively engage in the swallowing process. This active participation is crucial for their recovery and management of the condition.\",577\r\n3033,PACIENTE,LOGOPEDA,The logopeda evaluates and treats the patient for swallowing difficulties,557\r\n2894,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,LOGOPEDA,\"El logopeda trabaja en la rehabilitación de la deglución, lo cual es crucial para los niños que reciben nutrición enteral.\",346\r\n456,PACIENTES,DEGLUCIÓN,\"Patients often experience difficulties in the swallowing process, which requires targeted rehabilitation\",258\r\n1117,MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA,DEGLUCIÓN,\"The manual provides guidelines and analysis for the swallowing process, particularly in the context of dysphagia\",244\r\n662,NUTRICIÓN,DEGLUCIÓN,Nutrition is dependent on the successful process of deglución (swallowing),240\r\n1113,MANUAL